1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,228
For centuries, English had no dictionary at all.

2
00:00:03,228 --> 00:00:04,524
No rules for spelling.

3
00:00:04,524 --> 00:00:05,526
No list of words.

4
00:00:05,526 --> 00:00:06,999
Here is how that changed.

5
00:00:08,199 --> 00:00:12,589
In 1476, Caxton brings printing to England.

6
00:00:12,589 --> 00:00:18,306
In 1604, Cawdrey publishes the first English dictionary.

7
00:00:18,306 --> 00:00:22,900
In 1755, Samuel Johnson's dictionary arrives.

8
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:27,800
And in 1828, Noah Webster gives America its own.

9
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,892
Then, in 1928, the Oxford English Dictionary is finally complete.

10
00:00:33,892 --> 00:00:36,000
It took about seventy years.

11
00:00:37,199 --> 00:00:39,490
They spent seventy years collecting words.

12
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:41,290
You only need one new word a day.

13
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:43,200
Comment the word you learned today.

